-- title:
--   Finite-dimensionality of U-invariant matrix coefficients of I(χ)
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, so that $\mathbb{Q}_v$ denotes the $v$-adic completion, and write $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ for `LocalGL3 v`. Let $\chi = (\chi_0,\chi_1,\chi_2)$ be a triple of multiplicative homomorphisms $\mathbb{Q}_v^{\times} \to \mathbb{C}^{\times}$, and let `principalSeries3 v χ` be the $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions $f : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ that are locally constant, satisfy $f(u g) = f(g)$ for every upper unipotent matrix $u = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & x & z \\ 0 & 1 & y \\ 0 & 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ with $x,y,z \in \mathbb{Q}_v$ and every $g$, and satisfy $f(\mathrm{diag}(a_0,a_1,a_2)\,g) = \bigl(\prod_{i} \chi_i(a_i)\bigr)\cdot \bigl(\lVert a_0\rVert/\lVert a_2\rVert\bigr)\cdot f(g)$ for all units $a_i \in \mathbb{Q}_v^{\times}$ and all $g$. Let $\Lambda$ be any $\mathbb{C}$-linear form on this space, and for $f$ in it write $c_{\Lambda,f}(g) = \Lambda\bigl(h \mapsto f(hg)\bigr)$ for the associated matrix coefficient (`coefficientFn`). Let $U$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ whose underlying set is open. The assertion is that there exists a finite set $B$ of functions $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$, depending only on $v$, $\chi$, $\Lambda$ and $U$, such that for every $f$ in the principal series whose coefficient satisfies $c_{\Lambda,f}(gk) = c_{\Lambda,f}(g)$ for all $k \in U$ and all $g$, the function $c_{\Lambda,f}$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of $B$. No unitarity or irreducibility assumption is imposed on $\chi$, and the members of $B$ are not required to be matrix coefficients themselves.
--
--   This is the admissibility bound for the normalised principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over a $v$-adic field, in the form of a uniform finite-dimensionality statement for the space of matrix coefficients against a fixed linear form that are invariant under right translation by a given open subgroup. It supplies the finiteness input for the spanning and admissibility results about cyclic subspaces generated by spherical Whittaker functions of cubic inductions, and for the local Rankin–Selberg zeta computations attached to such coefficients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_finset_coefficientFn_mem_span_of_isOpen.lean

